  "notes": {
    "ReferenceKeys": "The handshake inputs are those of the open valid tests in handshake-xx.json and handshake-hfs.json: fixed labels in tools/reference.",
    "Replay": "Both sides run the group's handshake. Each then seals its frames in order as link records, a u16 length and then the ciphertext of the frame with empty associated data; its stream is those records back to back. After sealing the REKEY frame (05) a writer calls Rekey() on its sending cipher state; after opening one a reader calls Rekey() on its receiving cipher state; the nonce carries on. A BEARER_SWITCH frame (0f) changes no cipher state: the records after it continue the stream on the L2CAP CoC channel at the next nonce. A writer's own records equal its stream except at rejected_record. The responder must fail to open record rejected_record of initiator_stream and open every earlier one; every other record opens to its frame.",
    "OldKey": "The last record was sealed at the next nonce under the key before REKEY.",
    "Tampered": "One tag bit of the last record flipped in transit.",
    "NonceReset": "The first record after BEARER_SWITCH was sealed at nonce 0 with the same key, as if the cipher state restarted on the new bearer."
  },
